WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.460
Bye-bye, Batfleck.

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.600
This is the dawning of the age of Battinson.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.500
After much speculation about who would replace
Ben Affleck as Bruce Wayne in director Matt

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.920
Reeves' The Batman, we finally know who the
lucky actor is: Robert Pattinson.

00:00:12.129 --> 00:00:16.300
Sources close to Variety have noted that Pattinson,
who broke into the mainstream with the Twilight

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:20.350
franchise and has since gone on to make a
major name for himself in the drama genre

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:25.230
and with arthouse films, is in final negotiations
with studio Warner Bros. to top-line the feature

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.240
as the titular DC Comics hero.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.420
The ink on the contract hasn't dried just
yet, but the deal is expected to close soon.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.500
"It's hard to explain, but I need you to be
open-minded.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.580
Can you do that?"

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.640
Warner Bros. declined to comment on the news,
but it looks like Pattinson will take flight

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.190
to become the Caped Crusader before too long,
as The Batman is slated to start pre-production

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.180
sometime this summer and could go in front
of cameras either late this year or early

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:47.680
next.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.200
For many who've kept their fingers on the
pulse of all things related to The Batman,

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.810
learning that Pattinson is about to rise as
the new Bruce Wayne and assume the mantle

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:59.180
from Affleck, who dropped out of The Batman
as its director and its star, comes as little

00:00:59.180 --> 00:00:59.760
surprise.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.980
Rumors have been swirling for months now,
and at one point gained so much traction that

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:08.000
artists began crafting digital works envisioning
what the English actor would look like in

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.960
the Batsuit and dressed up in black-tie attire
as the billionaire Bruce Wayne.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:17.340
Other actors, including Armie Hammer, Logan
Lerman, Jack O'Connell, Ansel Elgort, Dylan

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:23.170
O'Brien, Aaron Taylor-Johnson, Noah Centineo,
Richard Madden, and Kit Harington, were reported

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.920
contenders for the leading role in The Batman,
but it's clear that Pattinson was the favorite.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:31.270
Warner Bros. and Reeves evidently love Pattinson
so much that they've tapped him before the

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:33.700
final version of the film's script is even
complete.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:38.630
It's true: Right now, Reeves is still polishing
the story before locking it in, but he apparently

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:40.760
couldn't wait to secure Pattinson before then.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.440
Reeves was said to be scouting for an actor
15 to 20 years younger than Affleck, who's

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.320
in his mid-40s.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.540
Pattinson fits that age range nicely.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:52.620
According to Variety, Warner Bros. is giving
Reeves as much time as needed to make The

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.040
Batman as perfect as possible, starting with
the script and the cast.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.780
The studio reportedly hopes that this version
of the famed DC vigilante makes up for how

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:05.300
the character was depicted in Batman v Superman:
Dawn of Justice and Justice League.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:09.720
Reeves previously described his take on the
iconic superhero as an "almost-noir driven,

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:13.400
detective version of Batman," and the film
as a whole as being influenced by the works

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.380
of Alfred Hitchcock.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.460
Reeves told The Hollywood Reporter in June
of 2017,

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.040
"What I try to do [...] is use the camera
and use the storytelling so that you become

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.760
that character, and you emphasize with that
point of view.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.660
There's a chance to do [a version of Batman]
that is point-of-view driven in a very, very

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:31.450
powerful way, that will hopefully connect
you to what's going on inside of his head

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.600
and inside of his heart."

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.860
To many, Pattinson is still and will always
be Edward Cullen from the Twilight saga.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.380
"This is who I am."

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:44.790
But the actor has done some genuinely fantastic
work in the time after the five-movie fantasy-romance

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.590
franchise wrapped in 2012.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:50.970
Pattinson went from glittering in the Washington
state sun as the brooding vampire, to dazzling

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.400
in films like The Lost City of Z, Good Time,
and High Life.

00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:58.840
Pattinson is set to appear in The Lighthouse,
The King, and Waiting for the Barbarians in

00:02:58.840 --> 00:02:59.960
2019 alone.

00:03:00.349 --> 00:03:04.540
The Batman is a project unlike anything Pattinson
has done in his career thus far, and it gives

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:08.730
the actor, whose biggest film role will likely
always precede him, a chance to show millions

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.780
of people who haven't kept up with his post-Twilight
work that he's more than just the vampire

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:13.280
guy.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:17.620
Pattinson does have a lot to live up to, since
many actors have played Batman before him,

00:03:17.629 --> 00:03:21.540
but the potent combination of his sharpened
acting chops, his status as a sort-of-underdog,

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.940
and the positive response his casting in The
Batman has already received hints that he'll

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:27.599
more than live up to expectations.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.680
"What are you?"

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.300
"I'm Batman."

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.640
The Batman hits theaters on June 25th, 2021.

